# Kept out of the release tarball packaging/archive.sh builds. What ships is
# what the installed daemon needs to run and the docs that explain it; the test
# suite, the release machinery itself, and working notes are not that.
#
# A directory named here has export-ignore set on the directory ENTRY, and
# `git archive` prunes the whole subtree. Note that `git check-attr` on a file
# INSIDE one still says "unspecified" — gitattributes patterns match the path
# they name, and unlike .gitignore a directory pattern does not extend over its
# contents. That is expected rather than broken, and it is subtle enough that
# archive.sh verifies the resulting tarball instead of trusting this file.
tests             export-ignore
pytest.ini        export-ignore
packaging         export-ignore
.github           export-ignore
plans             export-ignore
.roadmap_features export-ignore
.gitattributes    export-ignore
.gitignore        export-ignore
